---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { SITE } from '../data/site';
import { u } from '../lib/url';
---
<Base title={`Privacy | ${SITE.name}`} description={`${SITE.name} runs every calculator in your browser. No accounts, no tracking scripts, no uploads.`}>
  <div class="container" style="padding-top:32px">
    <nav class="breadcrumbs" aria-label="Breadcrumb"><a href={u('/')}>Home</a> / <span aria-current="page">Privacy</span></nav>
    <article class="prose">
      <h1>Privacy</h1>
      <p class="muted small">Last updated 30 October 2026</p>
      <p>{SITE.name} has no accounts, no ad scripts and no third-party trackers. Calculators run entirely in your browser. The menu engineering tool reads your sales file <strong>on your device</strong>; it is never uploaded.</p>
      <h2>Network requests this site makes</h2>
      <table>
        <thead><tr><th>Request</th><th>When</th><th>Contains your data?</th></tr></thead>
        <tbody><tr><td>Pages, scripts and styles</td><td>When you open a page</td><td>No</td></tr></tbody>
      </table>
      <p>Calculator inputs are stored only in the page address (so you can share a result). Nothing is sent to us. A strict <code>Content-Security-Policy</code> prevents scripts from sending data to other servers.</p>
      <h2>Affiliate links</h2>
      <p>Some pages recommend products through plain affiliate links. Clicking one takes you to the partner’s website, which applies its own privacy policy. A short tag only tells the partner which page of ours you came from. See our <a href={u('/disclosure/')}>affiliate disclosure</a>.</p>
      <h2>Cookies and analytics</h2>
      <p>The site sets no cookies. If privacy-friendly, cookie-free visit statistics are added in future (page views only, never your inputs), this page will be updated first. If advertising is ever added, it will use a certified consent banner where the law requires one.</p>
      <h2>Contact</h2>
      <p>Questions or a security concern? Contact {SITE.author} via the <a href={u('/about/#contact')}>About page</a>.</p>
    </article>
  </div>
</Base>
